{"name":"Pout","hex":"#e4ccc3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pout","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To push out one's lips; especially, to do so in a gesture of dismay, either serious or playful.","To thrust itself outward; to be prominent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One's facial expression when pouting.","A fit of sulking or sullenness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pout"}],"entries":[{"title":"Facial expression","blocks":[{"text":"Facial expression is a motion and positioning of the muscles beneath the skin of the face. These movements convey the emotional state of an individual to observers and are a form of nonverbal communication. They are a primary means of conveying social information between humans, but they also occur in most other mammals and some other animal species."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facial_expression"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lars_Jacob_as_Comedy_%26_Tragedy_1972.JPG/500px-Lars_Jacob_as_Comedy_%26_Tragedy_1972.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lars_Jacob_as_Comedy_%26_Tragedy_1972.JPG/500px-Lars_Jacob_as_Comedy_%26_Tragedy_1972.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An actor acting out Drama Masks (Thalia and Melpomene) in 1972","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALars_Jacob_as_Comedy_%26_Tragedy_1972.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/%D5%80%D5%B8%D6%82%D5%B5%D5%A6%D5%A5%D6%80.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/%D5%80%D5%B8%D6%82%D5%B5%D5%A6%D5%A5%D6%80.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Facial expressions help us recognize emotions","link":"https://en.wi